# mockcoding — environment variables

# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical public URL used for OG tags and absolute links.
# Override if you deploy to a custom domain.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in what you need. The hosted demo runs
# on the builder's own keys; self-hosters can leave provider keys empty and use
# the in-app "API Keys" (BYOK) drawer instead. All keys are read server-side
# only — never sent to the browser, logged, or persisted.

# ── AI providers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The default interviewer + feedback model is OpenAI, and OpenAI also powers
# voice (Whisper transcription + gpt-4o-mini-tts), so OPENAI_API_KEY is the one
# key the default demo needs. The others are selectable in the model menu / BYOK.

# OpenAI — interviewer, feedback, transcription, and (default) TTS.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional alternate interviewer / utility providers.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Voice / TTS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Engine select: "openai" (default, gpt-4o-mini-tts on OPENAI_API_KEY) or
# "elevenlabs". If TTS_PROVIDER is unset, ElevenLabs is used only when
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY is present, else OpenAI. To force OpenAI while an ElevenLabs
# key is also set, set TTS_PROVIDER=openai explicitly.
# TTS_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# OPENAI_TTS_VOICE=ash

# ElevenLabs — alternate TTS engine (optional).
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_flash_v2_5

# ── Code execution (Judge0) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to the public CE endpoint (https://ce.judge0.com), which is
# rate-limited / best-effort — fine for dev, will throttle at launch traffic.
# For launch, point at a paid or self-hosted instance and supply its auth header.
# JUDGE0_API_URL=
# JUDGE0_AUTH_HEADER_NAME=Authorization
# JUDGE0_AUTH_HEADER_VALUE=Bearer your-judge0-key
# For RapidAPI's Judge0 CE, the gateway needs the X-RapidAPI-Host header too:
#   JUDGE0_API_URL=https://judge0-ce.p.rapidapi.com
#   JUDGE0_AUTH_HEADER_NAME=X-RapidAPI-Key
#   JUDGE0_AUTH_HEADER_VALUE=your-rapidapi-key
#   JUDGE0_RAPIDAPI_HOST=judge0-ce.p.rapidapi.com

# ── Upstash Redis ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers per-IP rate limiting, signup capture, the launch funnel / rating stats,
# and the BYOK "at capacity" flag. Everything fail-open without it (no limiting,
# no analytics, BYOK off) — optional for local dev, recommended for launch.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── BYOK "at capacity" fallback ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# When active, new visitors are routed to /at-capacity to bring their own OpenAI
# key or join the waitlist, instead of spending the server key. It auto-trips on
# an OpenAI insufficient_quota error or when interview starts exceeds BYOK_SESSION_THRESHOLD (the
# sessions:started counter in Upstash). This var is an emergency manual override:
#   BYOK_MODE=on    force at-capacity ON
#   BYOK_MODE=off   force it OFF (overrides the Redis flag + the threshold) #recommended for local setup
# Leave unset for the automatic behavior.
BYOK_MODE=off

# Number of interview starts before auto-switching to BYOK (default: 225).
# BYOK_SESSION_THRESHOLD=

# ── Stats readout ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set any random string to enable GET /api/stats?token=<this> (funnel,
# signups-by-source, rating avg/distribution). Unset → the route 404s.
# STATS_TOKEN=
